    "body": "> Hi @nwaywood, can you run the following command in that directory and post the result\r\n> \r\n> ```shell\r\n> env STARSHIP_LOG=trace starship module git_status\r\n> ```\r\n\r\n@andytom I had the same problem and fixed it. Looks like the command is not mentionned in the documenation (maybe I missed it ?), in fact the documentation talks about the error logs `~/.cache/starship/session_${STARSHIP_SESSION_KEY}.log` but in my case, despite my problem it was empty. Don't know if it's normal or not.",
